    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "thanks for the tip on incorporation. one more thing though—it's kind of weird, even with the compost/blood meal, it feels like there's something else going on under the surface that we just can't see. sometimes it's like the nutrients just disappear or aren't being used the way they should be, even when the math says they are. do you think there's any hidden biological factor or some kind of unseen competition in the soil that could be messing with the efficiency?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
